<!-- Handoff industries/banking-financial-services.html: ask. Native Astro markup; shared document shell is V9Layout. -->
<section class="g-paper" id="ask">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow"><span class="tick">\</span> 03 · What we actually ask</div>
    <h2 style="--d:60ms">Three questions. Three thin answers.</h2>
    <p class="lead" style="--d:120ms">
      Every question comes off the candidate’s own CV, so these show the shape. The right-hand column is the part a
      generic interviewer can’t supply.
    </p>
    <div class="ix-qs">
      <article class="ix-q" style="--d:0ms">
        <span class="ab-k">Q1</span><h3>Walk me through a control that failed while you owned it.</h3><div
          class="ix-q-g"
        >
          <div>
            <span class="ix-lbl">A thin answer</span><p class="ix-thin">
              <span>“We had a reconciliation break. It was escalated and remediated within the window.”</span>
            </p>
          </div><div>
            <span class="ix-lbl">What the expert listens for</span><p>
              Who found it, how long it ran before anyone did, and what changed so it couldn’t recur. The remediation is
              the least interesting part of the answer.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article><article class="ix-q" style="--d:80ms">
        <span class="ab-k">Q2</span><h3>
          A core banking system returns stale balances under load. What do you do?
        </h3><div class="ix-q-g">
          <div>
            <span class="ix-lbl">A thin answer</span><p class="ix-thin">
              <span>“Add caching and retries, and raise it with the vendor.”</span>
            </p>
          </div><div>
            <span class="ix-lbl">What the expert listens for</span><p>
              Whether they reach for idempotency and reconciliation before retries, and whether they say out loud that a
              stale balance is a correctness problem a customer will see.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article><article class="ix-q" style="--d:160ms">
        <span class="ab-k">Q3</span><h3>Tell me about a time the regulation and the roadmap disagreed.</h3><div
          class="ix-q-g"
        >
          <div>
            <span class="ix-lbl">A thin answer</span><p class="ix-thin">
              <span>“We worked with compliance and found a path forward.”</span>
            </p>
          </div><div>
            <span class="ix-lbl">What the expert listens for</span><p>
              What was dropped. Somebody lost something in that conversation, and a person who was in it can tell you
              what and why.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
    <p class="decide">
      <b>A correct answer with no reasoning behind it proves nothing.</b> That line is written into how we score, and this
      sector is where it earns its keep.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
